WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.133
Ask who owns compliance and the
answer is often the security office,

2
00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:06.612
which really means nobody in particular.

3
00:00:06.612 --> 00:00:10.424
The Risk Management Framework
names an owner for every task.

4
00:00:10.424 --> 00:00:15.083
The system owner carries the most:
categorizing, implementing controls,

5
00:00:15.083 --> 00:00:19.663
fixing findings, keeping the plan of
action, and assembling the package.

6
00:00:19.663 --> 00:00:23.938
The CISO sets requirements and the
common controls systems inherit.

7
00:00:23.938 --> 00:00:28.000
The privacy official approves anything
touching personal information.

8
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.834
The authorizing official is the
only one who can accept the risk,

9
00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:33.425
and that can't be delegated.

10
00:00:33.425 --> 00:00:38.125
They also approve the plans and select
the assessor before the assessment starts.

11
00:00:38.125 --> 00:00:42.540
Several of these roles are government-only,
so a contractor-heavy team

12
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:46.650
can prepare every plan and package,
but can't sign those decisions.

13
00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:50.262
And keep the roles apart:
nobody assesses their own work.

14
00:00:50.262 --> 00:00:52.180
Now, the package itself.
